---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="How Local Flight Connects"
  description="See what stays on your home network, what each Local Flight mode sends online, whether Relay Access is needed, and where movement history is stored."
  active="network"
>
  <header class="terminal-hero terminal-hero--compact terminal-hero--text">
    <div class="terminal-frame terminal-grid hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy hero-copy--wide">
        <div class="eyebrow">How It Connects / Local and online paths</div>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Most of Local Flight stays on your network.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">The app, browsers, phones, and displays around your home talk to the computer running Local Flight. An internet connection is used only for the flight-data source you choose, phone-only Standalone, optional encrypted access away from home, or a report you submit.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="action-button action-button--primary" href="#paths">Compare every mode <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="action-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy design</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" id="paths">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="01 / CONNECTION MAP" title="Your Local Flight computer remains the centre of a home setup." description="Local screens connect directly. The selected flight-data path sits on the other side of the app, and optional Remote Companion passes only encrypted messages while you are away." />
      <div class="network-flow" data-reveal aria-label="Local Flight connections from a selected data source through the Local Flight computer to local and remote screens">
        <div class="network-flow-source"><span>CHOOSE ONE DATA PATH</span><strong>Beacon Relay</strong><strong>Your own provider keys</strong><strong>VATSIM</strong></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div class="network-flow-host"><span>RUNS ON YOUR HARDWARE</span><strong>Local Flight computer</strong><p>Settings, cached boards, history, logs, and display control stay here.</p></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div class="network-flow-screens"><span>YOUR SCREENS</span><strong>Desktop · LAN browser · kiosk</strong><strong>LED matrix · Companion</strong><p>These connections remain on your home or local network (LAN).</p></div>
        <div class="network-flow-remote"><span>OPTIONAL AWAY-FROM-HOME PATH</span><strong>Remote Companion</strong><p>End-to-end encrypted through Beacon Relay. The key stays on the paired phone and computer; Beacon Tools cannot read the message.</p></div>
        <small>Connection model · not live network activity</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--raised section--ruled">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="02 / MODE COMPARISON" title="See what connects, what leaves, and where history stays." description="Only the row for the mode you use applies. Relay Access is separate from the free Local Flight application." />
      <div class="mode-matrix" data-reveal>
        <div class="mode-matrix-row mode-matrix-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Mode</span><span>What connects</span><span>What leaves the device</span><span>Relay Access</span><span>History</span></div>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Desktop, LAN, matrix, Companion</strong><p>Local screens connect to your Local Flight computer.</p><p>Nothing for the screen connection itself.</p><span>No</span><p>On the Local Flight computer.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Beacon Relay</strong><p>The Local Flight computer connects to Beacon Relay.</p><p>Random service ID, device credential, airport and feature request.</p><span>Yes</span><p>On the Local Flight computer.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Bring Your Own Keys</strong><p>The Local Flight computer connects to your chosen provider.</p><p>The provider key and airport or aircraft request needed for the feature.</p><span>No</span><p>On the Local Flight computer.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Desktop VATSIM</strong><p>The Local Flight computer reads public VATSIM traffic.</p><p>Only the public data request; Local Flight avoids pilot and controller identity fields.</p><span>No</span><p>On the Local Flight computer.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Mobile VATSIM</strong><p>The phone reads public virtual-network data.</p><p>Only the public data request.</p><span>No</span><p>On the phone.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Real-flight Standalone</strong><p>The phone connects directly to Beacon Relay.</p><p>Random service ID, device credential, airport and feature request.</p><span>Yes</span><p>On the phone.</p></article>
        <article class="mode-matrix-row"><strong>Remote Companion</strong><p>The phone and licensed desktop host exchange messages through Beacon Relay.</p><p>Routing details and unreadable encrypted messages.</p><span>Uses host</span><p>On the Local Flight computer.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-footnote"><a href="/local-flight/relay-access/#why-paid">Why Beacon Relay is a paid hosted option</a>. Bring Your Own Keys and VATSIM remain available without Relay Access.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet section--ruled">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="03 / UPDATE TIMING" title="Why Local Flight may keep showing an older board." description="Aviation-data services have update limits and can be temporarily unavailable. Local Flight keeps a known board visible when it is more useful than an empty screen and shows when the data was last updated." />
      <div class="cadence-line" data-reveal>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>30 min</strong><h3>Desktop Beacon Relay board</h3><p>A Beacon Relay setup requests a new schedule board no more often than every 30 minutes.</p></article>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>About 1 h</strong><h3>Standalone board</h3><p>Real-flight Standalone requests new shared airline-schedule data about once an hour.</p></article>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>About 3 min</strong><h3>Standalone radar</h3><p>Nearby traffic can refresh about every three minutes while Radar is open.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-footnote">Between schedule checks, Standalone re-evaluates its saved board locally without requesting new airline data. VATSIM Standalone targets about one-minute board and Radar checks. Provider delays can keep an older board visible with its freshness time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="04 / TROUBLESHOOTING" title="Start with the mode shown in the app." description="The mode name tells you whether to check your home network, the computer running Local Flight, or the phone’s internet connection." />
      <ol class="troubleshooting-list" data-reveal>
        <li><span class="step">01 / HOME</span><strong>Companion on Wi-Fi</strong><p>Keep the phone and Local Flight computer on the same trusted network, confirm Local Flight is running, and scan the pairing code in Settings or enter the local address with port <code>:8000</code>.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">02 / AWAY</span><strong>Remote Companion</strong><p>Leave the licensed Local Flight computer online and connected to Beacon Relay. If access was revoked, return to the same home or local network and pair again.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">03 / PHONE</span><strong>Standalone</strong><p>Check the phone’s internet connection and wait a few minutes. A recent board may remain visible while a provider is unavailable.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">04 / SUPPORT</span><strong>Ask for help</strong><p>Include the mode, airport, approximate time, and whether the phone and computer were online. Include diagnostics only if you choose.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="inline-actions editorial-actions"><a class="action-button" href="/support/">Open Support</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SafetyNotice subject="Relay responses and cached board, radar, weather, and map data" />
</SiteLayout>
